tions of Wikipedia. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "The Pyramid of Djoser, completed around 2630 BCE during the Third Dynasty of Egypt, stands as a monumental achievement in ancient architecture, marking a pivotal moment in the evolution of pyramid construction. Located in Saqqara, the pyramid was designed by the architect Imhotep for Pharaoh Djoser, showcasing the innovative use of stone and establishing a template for subsequent pharaonic tombs. This structure represents a significant departure from the traditional mastaba tombs, symbolizing the transition to the grander pyramid structures that would define the Old Kingdom.

